  <title>Editing a product</title>

  <p>Click <gui>New</gui> or <gui>Edit</gui> in <link xref="products"/>, or
  <gui>Edit Product</gui> in the <link xref="product_hub"/>. Fill in the tabs
  and click <gui>Save</gui>, or press
  <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>S</key></keyseq>.
  <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Q</key></keyseq> closes the window without
  saving. Only one person can edit a product at a time; anyone else who opens
  it is told somebody else is editing it.</p>

  <section id="general">
  <title>General</title>
  <list>
    <item><p><gui>Name</gui> and <gui>Ext. name</gui> are what invoices and
    purchase orders show. When you leave the name, a warning icon appears if it
    does not follow your naming pattern; click it to see what is wrong and
    <gui>Use suggested name</gui>. The name can be saved either way. See <link
    xref="product_name_cleanup"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Barcode</gui> is the one you sell under. Vendors' barcodes go
    in <link xref="products#order_numbers">order numbers</link>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the unit it is sold in. <gui>Unit</gui> opens <link
    xref="units"/> to add one.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose its tax rate; <gui>Tax</gui> opens <link
    xref="tax_rates"/>. Uncheck <gui>Tax exemptible</gui> to charge tax on it
    even to a tax exempt customer.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="kind">
  <title>What the product is</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Sellable</gui></title>
    <p>Listed on invoices.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Purchasable</gui></title>
    <p>Listed on purchase orders. A product cannot be both purchasable and
    manufactured.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Manufactured</gui>, <gui>Job</gui></title>
    <p>Listed for manufacturing.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Invoice serial numbers</gui></title>
    <p>An invoice cannot be posted until each one sold has its serial
    number.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Stock</gui></title>
    <p>A stocked product. Unchecked, it is a non stock product, such as a
    service or a one-off item.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Track inventory</gui></title>
    <p>Counts how many are on hand, at each location, as they are bought,
    sold and made. It needs an inventory account.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts">
  <title>GL Accounts</title>
  <p>Choose the <gui>Expense account</gui> and <gui>Revenue account</gui>
  that buying and selling it post to, and the <gui>Inventory account</gui> if
  inventory is tracked. Type part of an account's name to find it. Enter the
  product's <gui>Cost</gui> here too.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="pricing">
  <title>Pricing</title>
  <p>Each customer markup term (see <link xref="customer_markup_percent"/>)
  has its own <gui>Markup %</gui> and <gui>Selling price</gui>. Change one and
  the other follows; changing the cost keeps each markup and recalculates the
  prices. A selling price cannot be set below cost. A customer is charged the
  price of their own markup term.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="inventory">
  <title>Inventory</title>
  <p><gui>Minimum stock</gui> and <gui>Reorder qty</gui> drive <link
  xref="products_to_reorder"/>. <gui>Current inventory (all locations)</gui>
  is how many are on hand. <gui>Adjust inventory</gui> corrects it; see <link
  xref="inventory_adjustment"/>.</p>
  <p>The <gui>Weights</gui> tab keeps the product's weight and tare, for
  shipping. <gui>Save window layout</gui> in the window menu remembers the
  window's size on this computer.</p>
  </section>

</page>
